==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Princess Juliet Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Juliet the Maiko''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
With her ability, some of her better usage is in [[Oncoming Maelstrom (Expert)|Oncoming Maelstrom]], to deal with the [[Divine Cyclone]] and the aggressive [[Stories of Legend]] angel pushers like [[Boraphim]]. Because of her stats and attack rate, a stack of Juliet Cats or combining her with other [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angels]] to permanently freeze them, or to inflict non-freeze effects.

That being said, she also has decent DPS and health, even rivaling that of [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], who is known to have great generalist stats, so any enemy with a range lower than her will be taken down fairly quickly.

However, her very long foreswing is often an issue, causing her to miss attacks and/or freeze effects as well as potentially having her knocked back or killed before attacking, greatly reducing her usage. She also sees extreme competition from a talented [[Sanzo Cat]]. Sanzo's rapid attacks, superior range and the slow effect is already able to cripple many angel pushers, leaving Juliet with little actual use.

==='''True Form'''===
Juliet the Maiko gains longer freeze time, lowered recharge time and 30 more range. The longer freeze and lowered recharge time both help with her effectiveness at freezing Angels. The 30 more range also puts her at a safer position when fighting a lot of enemies, but isn't really enough to make her outrange much more than she could in her previous forms, and she is still outclassed by Sanzo. Overall, this True Form makes her better than she already was, but only in her niche, and isn't of much priority.

The one specific use of her is to disable [[St. Dober]], as slow is woefully insufficient (units still move at a speed of 7.5 distance units per second) and cannot stop him from attacking or spawning surges.

==='''Talents'''===
Juliet the Maiko can become a lot better through [[talents]]: HP Buff and Attack Buff make her a better general attacker; speed could lead to her rushing to her death, but also opens her to new uses, [[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Knockback]] is useless as she is not recommended against [[Angelic Sleipnir|Sleipnir]]; and the improvement to her [[Freeze|Freeze]] duration makes her a much better staller. Once talented, this unit is much better at what she does, but the high competition and the necessity for a great investment of NP and [[Catseye]]s tend to make her not worth the trouble.

Note that level 1 of her Freeze talent, while only costing 10 NP, is responsible for about half of the effect. Therefore, it is recommended to just unlock this talent, as it is very cheap and helps greatly with keeping Juliet consistent.

